---
import LegalLayout from "../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Terms of Service — AzmFit"
  description="The rules of using AzmFit."
>
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: [DATE]</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>AzmFit is not a substitute for medical advice.</strong>
      Consult a qualified physician before starting any new exercise
      or diet program, especially if you have a medical condition,
      take medication, or are pregnant.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
  <p>
    By downloading, accessing, or using AzmFit ("the app," "the
    service"), you agree to these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you
    don't agree, don't use the app.
  </p>

  <h2>2. The service</h2>
  <p>
    AzmFit, operated by <strong>[COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME]</strong>, is an
    iOS app for tracking workouts, meals, body metrics, and weekly
    progress. Some features are free; others require an active
    Personal Pro or Coach Pro subscription.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You must create an account to use AzmFit. You're responsible for:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Providing accurate registration information.</li>
    <li>Keeping your password secure.</li>
    <li>All activity that happens under your account.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You must be at least 13 years old to use AzmFit. If you're between
    13 and 18, you affirm that your parent or guardian has reviewed
    and accepted these Terms on your behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Subscriptions and billing</h2>
  <p>
    Personal Pro and Coach Pro are auto-renewing subscriptions billed
    through your Apple ID at the rate shown at purchase. Subscriptions
    automatically renew unless you cancel at least 24 hours before
    the end of the current billing period.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can manage or cancel your subscription anytime in iOS
    Settings → [Your Name] → Subscriptions. Refunds are handled by
    Apple per their App Store policies — we cannot issue refunds
    directly.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Health and safety disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    AzmFit provides general fitness and nutrition tracking tools.
    It does not provide medical, nutritional, or therapeutic advice.
    The calorie and macro targets the app calculates are estimates
    based on standard formulas (Mifflin-St Jeor for calories,
    bodyweight ratios for protein, etc.) — they are not a personalized
    prescription.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Always consult a qualified physician or registered
    dietitian</strong> before starting a new exercise program,
    changing your diet significantly, or if you have any pre-existing
    medical condition. Stop exercising and seek medical attention if
    you feel dizzy, faint, short of breath, or experience pain.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Coaching relationships</h2>
  <p>
    AzmFit's coaching feature lets you connect with a third-party
    coach inside the app. We provide the platform that hosts this
    relationship — we are not party to the coaching agreement itself,
    we don't certify coaches, and we don't guarantee the quality or
    accuracy of any guidance a coach provides.
  </p>
  <p>
    Coaches you connect with may see workouts, meals, and metrics
    you log. You can end any coaching relationship from Settings at
    any time, which immediately revokes their access to your future
    data.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your content</h2>
  <p>
    Workouts, meals, photos, and notes you create in AzmFit are
    yours. You grant us a limited license to store, display, and
    process this content solely to provide the service to you (and
    to your coach if you have one). We will not use your content for
    advertising, training AI models, or any purpose outside running
    the app.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract source
      code from the app.</li>
    <li>Use the app to harass, threaten, or defraud anyone.</li>
    <li>Attempt to bypass usage limits or subscription tier checks.</li>
    <li>Use automated tools to scrape data from the app.</li>
    <li>Impersonate any person, including AzmFit staff.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The AzmFit name, logo, app, and all software, design, and
    content (excluding your own data) are owned by
    <strong>[COMPANY_LEGAL_NAME]</strong> and protected by copyright,
    trademark, and other laws. You may not copy, modify, or
    redistribute any part of the app without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using AzmFit at any time and delete your account
    from Settings. We may suspend or terminate your access if you
    violate these Terms or use the service in a way that harms
    others, the platform, or us. Upon termination, your data is
    deleted per our Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Disclaimers</h2>
  <p>
    The app is provided "as is" and "as available." We do not
    warrant that the service will be uninterrupted, bug-free, or that
    any calculation, recommendation, or AI-generated content will be
    accurate or suitable for your situation.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, AzmFit and
    its operators are not liable for any indirect, incidental,
    special, or consequential damages arising from your use of the
    service — including, without limitation, personal injury,
    nutritional miscalculations, missed training goals, or loss of
    data. Our total liability is capped at the amount you have paid
    us in the 12 months preceding the claim.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms are governed by the laws of [JURISDICTION], without
    regard to its conflict of laws principles. Any dispute will be
    resolved in the courts of [JURISDICTION].
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes
    will be announced in-app at least 30 days before they take
    effect. Continued use of the app after changes take effect
    constitutes acceptance.
  </p>

  <h2>15. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms? Email us at
    <strong>[CONTACT_EMAIL]</strong>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
